IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il40-nouns`

-- Sections 5 to 10: duties of the State; the official calendar; the national holiday and memorial days; the days of rest.  Row IL-40.
-- SEAT: the individual (NOTES.md section 1).  The text lists the days and calendars it names and does not close the list, so a day or a
-- calendar it does not name is answered NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-04: an unclosed list).

§ `Sections 5 to 10`

§§ `Sections 5, 6 and 7: duties of the State`

-- bl:34 | המדינה תהיה פתוחה לעלייה יהודית ולקיבוץ גלויות.
-- bl:38 | המדינה תשקוד על הבטחת שלומם של בני העם היהודי ושל אזרחיה הנתונים בצרה ובשביה בשל יהדותם או בשל אזרחותם.
-- bl:39 | המדינה תפעל בתפוצות לשימור הזיקה בין המדינה ובין בני העם היהודי.
-- bl:40 | המדינה תפעל לשימור המורשת התרבותית, ההיסטורית והדתית של העם היהודי בקרב יהדות התפוצות.
-- bl:43 | המדינה רואה בפיתוח התיישבות יהודית ערך לאומי, ותפעל על מנת לעודד ולקדם הקמה וביסוס שלה.
@ref Basic Law ss 5, 6(a), 6(b), 6(c), 7
GIVEN duty IS A `A duty the Basic Law puts on the State`
GIVETH A STRING
`the section that puts on the State the duty` duty MEANS
    CONSIDER duty
        WHEN `to be open to Jewish immigration and to the ingathering of exiles`                                                   THEN "s 5"
        WHEN `to endeavour to secure the safety of Jews and of citizens in distress or captivity because of their Jewishness or citizenship` THEN "s 6(a)"
        WHEN `to act in the Diaspora to preserve the bond between the State and Jews`                                              THEN "s 6(b)"
        WHEN `to act to preserve the cultural, historical and religious heritage of the Jewish people among Diaspora Jewry`        THEN "s 6(c)"
        WHEN `to act to encourage and promote the establishment and consolidation of Jewish settlement`                           THEN "s 7"

-- Section 6(a): the State "shall endeavour to secure the safety" of members of the Jewish people and of its citizens who are in distress or
-- in captivity "because of their Jewishness or their citizenship".  Fork F7: "because of their Jewishness or their citizenship" is read as
-- qualifying both groups.  The duty is to endeavour (תשקוד), not to secure.
@ref Basic Law s 6(a); NOTES.md fork F7
GIVEN `the person is Jewish` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a citizen of the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is in distress or in captivity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `because of the person's Jewishness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `because of the person's citizenship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 6(a) puts on the State the duty to endeavour to secure the safety of the person` MEANS
    IF (`the person is Jewish` OR `the person is a citizen of the State`) AND `the person is in distress or in captivity`
          AND (`because of the person's Jewishness` OR `because of the person's citizenship`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 8: the calendar`

-- bl:46 | הלוח העברי הוא לוח רשמי של המדינה ולצדו ישמש הלוח הלועזי כלוח רשמי; השימוש בלוח העברי ובלוח הלועזי ייקבע בחוק.
@ref Basic Law s 8
GIVEN calendar IS A `A calendar`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 8 makes the calendar an official calendar of the State` calendar MEANS
    CONSIDER calendar
        WHEN `the Hebrew calendar`    THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `the Gregorian calendar` THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `another calendar`       THEN NOTHING

§§ `Section 9: the national holiday and the memorial days`

-- bl:50 | יום העצמאות הוא יום החג הלאומי הרשמי של המדינה.
-- bl:52 | יום הזיכרון לחללי מערכות ישראל ויום הזיכרון לשואה ולגבורה הם ימי זיכרון רשמיים של המדינה.
@ref Basic Law s 9(a), (b)
GIVEN day IS A `A day the Basic Law speaks of`
GIVETH A MAYBE `A standing the Basic Law gives to a day`
`the standing s 9 gives to` day MEANS
    CONSIDER day
        WHEN `Independence Day`                                      THEN JUST `the official national holiday of the State`
        WHEN `Memorial Day for the fallen of Israel's wars`          THEN JUST `an official memorial day of the State`
        WHEN `Holocaust and Heroism Remembrance Day`                 THEN JUST `an official memorial day of the State`
        WHEN `the Sabbath`                                           THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `a festival of Israel`                                  THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `another day`                                           THEN NOTHING

§§ `Section 10: the days of rest`

-- bl:56 | שבת ומועדי ישראל הם ימי המנוחה הקבועים במדינה; למי שאינם יהודים זכות לקיים את ימי המנוחה בשבתם ובחגיהם; פרטים לעניין זה ייקבעו בחוק.
@ref Basic Law s 10
GIVEN day IS A `A day the Basic Law speaks of`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10 makes the day one of the fixed days of rest of the State` day MEANS
    CONSIDER day
        WHEN `the Sabbath`                                           THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `a festival of Israel`                                  THEN JUST TRUE
        WHEN `Independence Day`                                      THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `Memorial Day for the fallen of Israel's wars`          THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `Holocaust and Heroism Remembrance Day`                 THEN NOTHING
        WHEN `another day`                                           THEN NOTHING

-- The right is given "to those who are not Jews"; for a Jew the sentence is silent.  Who is a Jew is not answered here: it is a fact the
-- person states (fork F8).  The details are left to "a law": the Law and Administration Ordinance s 18A(a) leaves a non-Jew's festivals to a
-- Government decision published in Reshumot (aid; not part of this encoding).
@ref Basic Law s 10; NOTES.md fork F8
GIVEN `the person is Jewish` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10 gives the person the right to keep the days of rest on their own Sabbath and festivals` MEANS
    IF `the person is Jewish` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST TRUE
